<title>USA: August Brent inches up in late U.S. paper trading.</title>
<headline>August Brent inches up in late U.S. paper trading.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>North Sea Brent inched up in late U.S. paper trading on Wednesday, traders said.</p>
<p>A full boat of August Brent traded at $17.70, up five cents from the IPE settlement.</p>
<p>Four partial cargoes moved, twice at $17.68 and twice at $17.69.</p>
<p>July/August Brent changed hands at minus 28 and minus 29 cents.</p>
<p>August/September was pegged around minus 24-21 cents, while September/October was at minus 19-15 cents.</p>
<p>--Patricia Garip-Bertuol NY Energy Desk ((+1 212 859 1620))</p>
